course: dictionary
lesson: 6573
title: One word, two meanings: nightingale
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: A nightingale is a small brown bird. Its song is loud, beautiful and varied, and it often sings at night as well as in the day. In «Bringing missing animals back ... in Britain it has brought back beavers, white storks and nightingales», the word is a common noun for a bird, a creature you could see and hear.
explain: Look at the capital letter in Nightingale. Florence Nightingale is a name, a proper noun for one real person. She was an English nurse in Victorian times, and she was called «the Lady with the Lamp». The capital letter is your first clue that the word is a name.
explain: Context tells you which meaning is meant. In a nature text, a nightingale is a bird. In a history lesson, Nightingale is a person. In a poem or story, «a nightingale voice» means a lovely singing voice. Ask yourself what the sentence is about, then try your meaning in it.
fact: A nightingale is a small brown bird known for its loud, beautiful song.
fact: Nightingales often sing at night as well as in the day.
fact: At Knepp in England, «storks, turtle doves and nightingales came back» after a farm was left to go wild.
fact: Florence Nightingale was an English nurse in Victorian times who made hospitals cleaner.
fact: Nightingale is also a name for a person, so it starts with a capital letter.
exercise: «Bringing missing animals back ... brought back beavers, white storks and nightingales.» In this sentence, what is a nightingale? | A kind of tree | A nurse in a hospital | *A small brown bird | A sad song
exercise: Florence Nightingale was called «the Lady with the Lamp». What kind of word is Nightingale here? | A word for a quiet night | A type of lamp | *A name for one person | A bird that lives in towns
exercise: «The nightingale sang all night in the garden.» What does nightingale mean here? | A type of garden gate | A nurse who cared for soldiers | A kind of old boat | *A small brown bird with a loud, beautiful song
test: «Her nightingale voice filled the whole hall.» What does nightingale mean here? | *A lovely singing voice | A nurse who calls out orders | A type of hall | A bird that lives in the hall
test: Which sentence uses Nightingale as a name? | The nightingale built its nest in the hedge | Nightingales sing at night in spring | The nightingale is a small brown bird | *Florence Nightingale helped to make hospitals cleaner
exam: Why does the capital letter matter when you read Nightingale? | *It shows it is a name, a proper noun for one person | It means the word is in a poem | It shows the sentence is a question | It shows the bird is important
